it's a big deal --
to what happened on January 6,

00:10:18.751 --> 00:10:21.153 line:0%
when you had this
insurrection at the Capitol?

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:22.488 line:0%
-You had an insurrection
in the Capitol.

00:10:22.488 --> 00:10:24.223 line:0%
You've had political violence

00:10:24.223 --> 00:10:25.758 line:0%
for the last year,
in this building.

00:10:25.758 --> 00:10:27.993 line:0%
You had, a Good Friday,
an officer killed

00:10:27.993 --> 00:10:31.263 line:0%
for political belief,
right on that Capitol as well.

00:10:31.263 --> 00:10:33.132 line:0%
If you're now going to put
a commission together,

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:35.868 line:0%
why wouldn't you look at all
the problems to solve --

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:37.869
-Oh, you want a commission
to look at all the problems?

00:10:37.869 --> 00:10:39.004
Then, while we're at it,

00:10:39.004 --> 00:10:40.806
can we have the commission
investigate this?

00:10:40.806 --> 00:10:42.608
-I want you to watch
Nancy Pelosi

00:10:42.608 --> 00:10:43.676
hand me that gavel.

00:10:43.676 --> 00:10:46.111
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:10:46.111 --> 00:10:49.781
And I promise you this --

00:10:49.781 --> 00:10:51.684
I won't bang her with it,

00:10:51.684 --> 00:10:55.788
but I'll bang the end to the
socialism, and yes to America.

00:10:55.788 --> 00:10:57.990
-That is one of the weirdest
sentences I've ever heard,

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.491
and I work near Times Square.

00:10:59.491 --> 00:11:00.659
Do you know how often

00:11:00.659 --> 00:11:02.561
I've had German tourists
come up to me and ask...?

00:11:02.561 --> 00:11:04.530
[ German accent ]
Can you tell where's
the headquarters

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:06.565
of ze little
chocolate candy man?

00:11:06.565 --> 00:11:08.233
"Sorry,
you mean the M&amp;M's store?"

00:11:08.233 --> 00:11:10.569
[ German accent ]
Ja. We want to meet
the sexy one.

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:12.237
[ Laughter ]

00:11:12.237 --> 00:11:14.039
[ Irish accent ]
I wouldn't mind, either.
I'm from Iceland.

00:11:14.039 --> 00:11:16.174
[ Laughter ]

00:11:16.174 --> 00:11:19.311
Do you mind giving me
a w-w-wee bit of directions?

00:11:19.311 --> 00:11:20.746
[ Laughter ]

00:11:20.746 --> 00:11:22.715
You can't just take a commission
about an insurrection,

00:11:22.715 --> 00:11:24.783
a very specific
and horrifying event

00:11:24.783 --> 00:11:26.018
in the history of this country,
and make it

00:11:26.018 --> 00:11:27.386
about whatever you want,

00:11:27.386 --> 00:11:29.421
just to score dumb political
points with your base.

00:11:29.421 --> 00:11:31.623
When Republicans spent a year
investigating Benghazi,

00:11:31.623 --> 00:11:33.959
Democrats weren't like,
"Hey, while we're at it,

00:11:33.959 --> 00:11:36.462
could we also investigate what
Harrison Ford's been smoking?"

00:11:36.462 --> 00:11:39.598
Whatever that strain is,
let's legalize that [bleep] now.

00:11:39.598 --> 00:11:41.067
It's like my man went
to Union Station

00:11:41.067 --> 00:11:42.801
to catch a train
and only then found out

00:11:42.801 --> 00:11:44.136
they were hosting the Oscars.

00:11:44.136 --> 00:11:45.170
"Hey, since you're here,

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:46.372
you want to give one out
for editing?"

00:11:46.372 --> 00:11:48.740
[ As Ford ]
Sure, I do carry around these

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.709
"Blade Runner" editing notes.

00:11:50.709 --> 00:11:52.545
[ Laughter ]
And there's a lot more
we need to find out

00:11:52.545 --> 00:11:54.213
about what, exactly, happened
on that day,

00:11:54.213 --> 00:11:55.614
which is why we need
a commission

00:11:55.614 --> 00:11:57.683
singularly focused
on the insurrection.

00:11:57.683 --> 00:11:59.885
For example, one of the few
Republican members of Congress

00:11:59.885 --> 00:12:03.422
who voted to impeach Trump
has said that McCarthy told her

00:12:03.422 --> 00:12:05.390
about a conversation
he had with Trump

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:06.692
in the middle of the riot,

00:12:06.692 --> 00:12:09.328
in which Trump seemed
to justify the insurrection.

00:12:09.328 --> 00:12:10.629
-This is actually part of the

00:12:10.629 --> 00:12:12.397
impeachment record,
the second impeachment.

00:12:12.397 --> 00:12:16.402
This was read
into the record there...

00:12:26.945 --> 00:12:29.448
-I mean, I suppose that's true,
but it's a little like saying,

00:12:29.448 --> 00:12:30.682
"Well, I guess these zombies

00:12:30.682 --> 00:12:32.484
enjoy eating brains more
than you do."

00:12:32.484 --> 00:12:34.720
So, clearly,
Trump supported the attack,

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:36.254
as if we needed
any more evidence.

00:12:36.254 --> 00:12:37.822
He would've been
perfectly happy,

00:12:37.822 --> 00:12:40.025
if the mob had successfully
taken over the Capitol,

00:12:40.025 --> 00:12:41.627
stopped the counting
of electoral votes,

00:12:41.627 --> 00:12:43.195
and allowed him
to overturn the results.

00:12:43.195 --> 00:12:45.197
Saying Trump didn't know
anything about it

00:12:45.197 --> 00:12:46.831
is like saying Glenn Close

00:12:46.831 --> 00:12:48.200
doesn't know how to do Da Butt.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.734
Second Oscars joke.

00:12:49.734 --> 00:12:51.036
Look, we follow the buzz, okay?

00:12:51.036 --> 00:12:52.404
That's what people
are talking about,

00:12:52.404 --> 00:12:53.405
so that's what we
write jokes about.

00:12:53.405 --> 00:12:55.040
No more "M-A-S-H" references.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.110
No more jokes
about Vince Vaughn-Owen Wilson

00:12:58.110 --> 00:12:59.778
buddy comedies
from 20 years ago.

00:12:59.778 --> 00:13:01.980
From now on, it is all fresh,

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:05.251
topical, pop culture references
here at "Late Night."

00:13:05.251 --> 00:13:07.753
Anyway, McCarthy was asked
if that account

00:13:07.753 --> 00:13:09.855
of his conversation
with Trump was accurate

00:13:09.855 --> 00:13:11.624
and McCarthy refused to say.

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:13.893
-Is that what President Trump
said to you?

00:13:13.893 --> 00:13:15.561
-When I talked
to President Trump about it,

00:13:15.561 --> 00:13:17.263 line:0%
I was the first person
to contact him

00:13:17.263 --> 00:13:19.364 line:0%
when the riot was going on.
He didn't see it.

00:13:19.364 --> 00:13:21.466 line:0%
What he ended the call
was saying, telling me,

00:13:21.466 --> 00:13:24.436 line:0%
he'll put something out
to make sure to stop this.

00:13:24.436 --> 00:13:27.038 line:0%
And that's what he did,
he put a video out later.

00:13:27.038 --> 00:13:28.139 line:0%
-Quite a lot later.

00:13:28.139 --> 00:13:29.607 line:0%
And it was a pretty weak video.

00:13:29.607 --> 00:13:32.110 line:0%
But I'm asking you specifically,
did he say to you,

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.746 line:0%
"I guess some people
are more concerned

00:13:33.746 --> 00:13:36.081 line:0%
about the election
than you are?"

00:13:36.081 --> 00:13:38.183 line:0%
-No, listen, my conversations
with the president

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.751 line:0%
are my conversations
with the president.

00:13:39.751 --> 00:13:41.220
-Wow, he avoided that question

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.021
like he was Vince Vaughn
in "Dodgeball."

00:13:43.021 --> 00:13:44.622
[ As Vaughn ]
Buddy, buddy, buddy,
you're killing me, here.

00:13:44.622 --> 00:13:46.491
I would never divulge
a private conversation.

00:13:46.491 --> 00:13:47.826
I'm a discreet guy.

00:13:47.826 --> 00:13:49.194
You know that about me.

00:13:49.194 --> 00:13:50.963
Do I gossip occasionally?
Sure.

00:13:50.963 --> 00:13:52.398
Would I let a secret slip,
here and there,

00:13:52.398 --> 00:13:53.799
in return for a favor?
Who wouldn't?

00:13:53.799 --> 00:13:55.200
But I tell you, I would never

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:57.669
tell someone else
what you told me in confidence.

00:13:57.669 --> 00:13:58.938
Not now, not ever.

00:13:58.938 --> 00:14:01.073
[ As Wilson ]
Alright. Wow, man. Right on.

00:14:01.073 --> 00:14:02.541
[ Laughter ]
Owen Wilson wasn't
in "Dodgeball,"

00:14:02.541 --> 00:14:03.708
but, I mean,
he should've been, right?

00:14:03.708 --> 00:14:05.544
So I lied, when I said

00:14:05.544 --> 00:14:07.579
[ Laughter ]
our references, from now on,
would be fresh.

00:14:07.579 --> 00:14:09.582
Much like Kevin McCarthy lied
in that answer.

00:14:09.582 --> 00:14:10.649
Segue!

00:14:10.649 --> 00:14:12.251
Because, first of all,
[ Laughter ]

00:14:12.251 --> 00:14:14.152
there's no way Trump didn't know
what was going on

00:14:14.152 --> 00:14:15.354
until McCarthy called him.

00:14:15.354 --> 00:14:17.622 line:0%
We have contemporaneous
accounts telling us

00:14:17.622 --> 00:14:19.458 line:0%
Trump was watching it all
unfold on TV

00:14:19.458 --> 00:14:22.027 line:0%
and gleefully egging it on
and, even if we didn't

00:14:22.027 --> 00:14:24.529 line:0%
have those accounts,
we'd still know

00:14:24.529 --> 00:14:28.000 line:0%
that Trump was aware of the
insurrection as it was happening

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.602 line:0%
because he's always watching TV.

00:14:30.602 --> 00:14:33.472 line:0%
Honestly, I'm not sure
why it never occurred to us,

00:14:33.472 --> 00:14:35.507 line:0%
but we could've avoided
his presidency

00:14:35.507 --> 00:14:37.809 line:0%
by just planting him
in front of the wall of TVs

00:14:37.809 --> 00:14:39.745 line:0%
at Circuit City for four years.

00:14:39.745 --> 00:14:41.679
[ As Trump ]
Circuit City, folks.
They love us there.

00:14:41.679 --> 00:14:42.848
Won it in a landslide.

00:14:42.848 --> 00:14:44.249
Sadly, it wasn't enough

00:14:44.249 --> 00:14:46.284
to overcome
all the fraudulent votes

00:14:46.284 --> 00:14:47.553
from The Wiz.

00:14:47.553 --> 00:14:49.154
That's why nobody
beats them, folks.

00:14:49.154 --> 00:14:50.355
[ Laughter ]
It's all a fraud.

00:14:50.355 --> 00:14:52.323
But what a slogan.
What a slogan.

00:14:52.323 --> 00:14:54.727
We used to have the best
slogans, didn't we, folks?

00:14:54.727 --> 00:14:57.062
What happened to all
our beautiful slogans?

00:14:57.062 --> 00:14:59.898
Got to go to Mos,
Mos Def, Def Comedy Jam.

00:14:59.898 --> 00:15:01.066
[ Laughter ]
Jam!

00:15:01.066 --> 00:15:02.434
We love jam, don't we, folks?

00:15:02.434 --> 00:15:04.602
Smucker's
[ Laughter ]

00:15:04.602 --> 00:15:07.539
sounds dirty.
Not. Not dirty.

00:15:07.539 --> 00:15:10.209
"With a name like Smucker's,
it's got to be good."

00:15:10.209 --> 00:15:11.210
[ Laughter ]

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:13.345
That's what they say.
It's true.

00:15:13.345 --> 00:15:16.481
But you can't buy it anymore.
That's what I hear.

00:15:16.481 --> 00:15:18.350
They canceled Smucker's.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.519
[ Laughter ]
I haven't been to a store
in years.

00:15:20.519 --> 00:15:21.587
I don't know
if that's true, but.

00:15:21.587 --> 00:15:23.054
[ Laughter ]

00:15:23.054 --> 00:15:26.958
Also, Trump didn't put a video
out to stop anything.

00:15:26.958 --> 00:15:28.993
He told the rioters,
"We love you.

00:15:28.993 --> 00:15:29.995
You're very special."

00:15:29.995 --> 00:15:31.330
One of those weird,

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.631
outdoor videos of his
on the White House lawn,

00:15:33.631 --> 00:15:36.134
where he looks like
he's filming a YouTube tutorial

00:15:36.134 --> 00:15:38.136
on how to properly
trim your hedges.

00:15:38.136 --> 00:15:39.737
This is one
of the central themes

00:15:39.737 --> 00:15:41.639
of our politics, at the moment.
The Republican Party

00:15:41.639 --> 00:15:44.476
is an increasingly paranoid,
authoritarian movement,

00:15:44.476 --> 00:15:47.379
defending a president
who incited an insurrection

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:49.180
and spreading unhinged lies
about everything

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:51.950
from life-saving vaccines
to imaginary bans on red meat.

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:53.919
I mean, it's almost like
all these guys are drunk on...

00:15:53.919 --> 00:15:55.721
-Plant-based beer.

00:15:55.721 --> 00:15:57.222
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:15:57.222 --> 00:16:00.926
♪♪

00:16:00.926 --> 00:16:02.427
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:16:02.427 --> 00:16:03.728
